{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LATE FINDINGS (2026-08-07, after the verification sweep)\n\n7084 LOCK WORK LANDED — R5 (1507), R1 (1508), R3 (1510), all merged with both gates green. R1 measured on a 71,041-commit clone: 4-file ticket 29.81s->1.05s (28x); 25 files 193.16s->4.72s (41x); 73 files 546.00s->4.27s (128x); 155 files 1165.54s->2.09s (557x); zero mismatches across 257 events. The material change is that the AFTER column does not grow with event count — cost is now per-compaction, not per-event, so the unbounded growth is gone. Equivalence proven four ways including an explicit off-first-parent fixture (same event added on both sides of a merge, so the merge is TREESAME to both parents; the test asserts the simplified query returns something DIFFERENT, so the fixture cannot silently stop exercising the case). 7084 left in_progress: R3's floor question, the terminal-and-lossy acquire budget, and post-R1 re-measurement under the 6-writer harness are all still open.\n\n858c STATUS REVERSION — ROOT-CAUSED, NOT A REGRESSION FROM THIS SESSION. Inbound wrote a real newer STATUS event authored by 'reconciler'; the reducer was never wrong. Mechanism: _advance_baselines advances from the PASS-START snapshot taken before the outbound apply, so in the pass where rebar pushes a status the baseline keeps the OLD value. A reopen is a revert to a previous value and lands exactly in that window: local 'open' equals the stale baseline, outbound suppresses, inbound then mirrors Jira's stale 'closed' back. Description survived because it DIFFERED from the stale baseline and was pushed; status was clobbered because it EQUALLED it. Timing is decisive: the clobbering pass ran 10:14:54Z, every suspect commit landed 12:16Z-13:13Z. Identical shape found on 2026-07-20 across 8 tickets, 18 days earlier. Self-limiting (baseline advances after a clobber, next pass pushes local out) so no bridge pause needed. Filed as e6e9-ddbf-223b-4f49 (P1). AWAITING OPERATOR DECISION between fix A (advance the baseline to what was actually pushed) and fix B (state fields never lose to inbound).\n\nCOVERAGE GAP behind it: ADR 0026 mandates a direction-preservation cell and it exists for 'title' ONLY. The status equivalent drives adapters/jira/outbound_fields._diff_fields, which has NO PRODUCTION CALLER — status has never been pinned on the live path.\n\nTHIRD INSTANCE of the same class today: 599e (38 tests across 11 files passing by NOT RUNNING), 24f7 (a tree-wide check that was a manual grep, not a committed test), and now a test exercising a function nothing calls. All three looked like coverage and were not.\n\nSECOND REGRESSION FROM 0767c38ebb (63e8) reaching main within hours: canary_bridge.py:31 does a bare 'import alert_dedup' that resolves only when scripts/ is on sys.path, so subset test runs error (2 errors, CI's full run green). Filed as 291e-7b48-3f24-41c6, linked discovered_from 63e8. Same defect class as a371, whose guard covers 'tests.'-rooted imports under tests/ but NOT bare imports of scripts/ modules — the class is half-guarded."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786122907329291001,"uuid":"e585d88e-6154-42ee-966d-12c6f55bd73f"}